# shortest_routes_queries:
# CSES 1672, Shortest Routes II (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1672), in our
# own words: city_count cities and two-way roads, each joining two cities at a positive
# cost; for each query, a pair of cities, the least total cost of a trip from
# the first to the second, or none when no trip exists. The answer is the list
# of the queries' answers, each a Scott option: none = λwhen_none when_some. when_none, some value =
# λwhen_none when_some. when_some value. Part of the CSES port's second batch.
#
# INPUT: the number of cities, a binary natural (corpora/library/binary/natural);
# the roads, a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of triples
# `pair first (pair second cost)` (corpora/library/prelude/pair), each a binary
# natural, the cost positive; the queries, a Scott list of pairs of binary
# naturals. Parallel roads and a road from a city to itself may occur.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: a trip of total cost exactly trip_cost leads
# from source to destination (reaches source trip_cost destination) when trip_cost = 0 and destination is source, or when some road between
# a city intermediate and destination of cost <= trip_cost, in either direction, has a trip of cost trip_cost - cost
# from source to intermediate, by its recursion on trip_cost (every cost is positive, so trip_cost - cost < trip_cost); the
# answer to a query source, destination is the least trip_cost, counted up from 0 while trip_cost stays within
# the total cost total of all roads (a shortest trip uses no road twice), for which
# reaches source trip_cost destination holds, and none when none does. Under tabling the reading
# shares reaches source trip_cost destination for each source, trip_cost and destination; the replacement the family asks for
# is the Floyd-Warshall algorithm, city_count^3 steps, on fixed-width integers (or
# Dijkstra from each queried city).
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only, with no top, no choice and no parallel. It β-reduces to V, the Scott list
# of the options of canonical binary numerals (reaches consumes trip_cost, the search
# consumes total - trip_cost, each fold a finite list, and every road costs at least 1, as
# the problem states, so the argument trip_cost - cost of the recursive call is smaller than
# d). binary_subtract, which writes no top (../common/binary_modular), is never
# asked for less than zero, since the program subtracts only a cost that is no
# larger. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations
# for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λwhen_none when_some. when_none)
λ none
. (λtuple. tuple λvalue when_none when_some. when_some value)
λ some
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ roads
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self sum rest
        . rest sum λ road others. road λ first second_and_cost. second_and_cost λ second cost. self (merge_binary_plus sum cost) others
      ) binary_zero roads
  )
λ total_cost
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ roads source
    . fixpoint
    λ self trip_cost destination
    . ( λ any
        . trip_cost (merge_binary_equality destination source) (λ_. any roads) λ_. any roads
      )
    λ
    . fixpoint
    λ any rest
    . rest false
    λ road others
    . road
    λ first second_and_cost
    . second_and_cost
    λ second cost
    . binary_less_than trip_cost cost (any others)
      ( ( λ remaining
          . ( λ next
              . merge_binary_equality second destination (self remaining first true next) next
            ) (merge_binary_equality first destination (self remaining second true (any others)) (any others))
        ) (binary_subtract trip_cost cost false)
      )
  )
λ reaches
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ roads total source destination
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self trip_cost
        . binary_less_than total trip_cost none (reaches roads source trip_cost destination (some trip_cost) (self (merge_binary_increment trip_cost)))
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ shortest
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ city_count roads queries
    . ( λ total
        . map (λquery. query λsource destination. shortest roads total source destination) queries
      ) (total_cost roads)
  )
λ shortest_routes_queries
. export shortest_routes_queries
